  "body": "What changed\n\nA non-centre-cutting tool with the Arc entry and a None lead-in is refused at the grazing dive in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_step.rs`. The refusal is correct. Its hint was wrong.\n\nOld text (after the prefix \"entry refused: the tool is not centre-cutting\"):\n`the dive at the lead-in (x, y) is into material no helix or ramp can be proved beside; pick the Arc entry or a centre-cutting tool`\n\nNew text for the Arc entry with a None lead-in:\n`the dive at the lead-in (x, y) is into material no helix or ramp can be proved beside; the Arc entry does not run when the lead-in is None; set a Linear or Arc lead-in, or use a centre-cutting tool`\n\nThe same dive is also reached by the Arc entry when no arc fits beside the wall, or on a tabbed level. There the hint is now: `the Arc entry found no room here (see the entry note); use a centre-cutting tool`. The other entries keep the old hint.\n\nThe refusal condition (`!a.center_cutting`) is unchanged. No program that was refused is now accepted, and no program that was accepted is now refused. The change is the hint text, and `graze` takes the entry as a new parameter.\n\nReadings\n\n- No golden file and no other test holds the old text (searched `crates`, `tests`, `docs`, `site`, `testdata`).\n- Pinning test: `arc_entry_with_no_lead_in_refuses_a_non_centre_cutting_tool_and_names_the_lead_in` in `crates/app/tests/contour_none_lead.rs`. It checks that the refusal prefix stands, that the new words are present, and that \"pick the Arc entry\" is absent.\n- Passed: that test alone; the whole `contour_none_lead` binary (5 tests); `camcraft-motion` lib `machining2d` (252 passed, 10 ignored); `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (5 steps, 0 failed); clippy `-D warnings` for `camcraft-motion --all-targets` and for `camcraft-app --test contour_none_lead`.\n\nNot exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes ran after the first version of this body: see the section \"Heavy lanes\" below (242 steps, 0 failed). No heavy test holds the old text.\n- The batch tier runs in the post-merge gate.\n- No application window was started.\n\n## Heavy lanes (run by a gate-runner after the first quick pass)\nA gate-runner ran `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main` on head 3c6192f1e09dae51356805dfee134cddb7e46250. The change reaches the `motion heavy` lane and the `app heavy` lane. 242 steps ran in release, and 0 steps failed. The run took 62.5 minutes. Four tests are known-fail tests (#1950 three times, #2849 one time). They failed as expected, and the gate shows each one as \"known fail, red as expected\". The light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`) ran 2 light twins: `the_slot_keeps_its_verdict_under_sub_micron_perturbations_light` and `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes_light`. The two passed. No golden file changed. The test binary `contour_none_lead` has no ignored test, so it has no heavy step. No step of the plan was left unrun.\n\nChangelog: A contour with the Arc entry and no lead-in now tells a user of a non-centre-cutting tool to set a lead-in, instead of telling them to pick the Arc entry.\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3247\n\n\n",
